# Local data artifacts — regenerate with `npm run pipeline`
data/*.sqlite
data/*.sqlite-journal
data/cache/

# apps/web/public/data is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It was, until this project was deployed to a static host. A host that builds
# from this repository runs `npm run build`, which compiles the app and does not
# run the pipeline — so the deployed site came up with the app shell and no data
# behind it, showing the "there is no data here yet" card to every visitor.
#
# The alternative was running the whole pipeline inside the host's build. That
# would mean re-downloading hundreds of megabytes from the FEC and GovInfo on
# every deploy, a build that fails when a government API has a bad afternoon,
# and — worst for this project specifically — figures that change silently
# underneath readers between deploys. For a tool whose entire claim is that
# every number traces to a named filing, the dataset being a committed,
# diffable, pinned artifact is a feature and not a workaround.
#
# Cost of that choice, stated plainly: about 76 MB across ~2,550 files, of which
# 29 MB is the 524 member portraits. Refreshing the data is `npm run pipeline`
# followed by a commit, and the diff is reviewable.
#
# The mobile bundle below stays ignored: nothing deploys it, and an Expo build
# regenerates it from the same pipeline.
apps/mobile/assets/data/**/*.json
!apps/mobile/assets/data/.gitkeep

# OS noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

